  "title": "Erdős Problem #792",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n)$ be maximal such that in any $A\\subset \\mathbb{Z}$ with $\\lvert A\\rvert=n$ there exists some sum-free subset $B\\subseteq A$ with $\\lvert B\\rvert \\geq f(n)$, so that there are no solutions to $ a+b=c $ with $a,b,c\\in B$. Estimate $f(n)$.",
